{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>I have become small from all the kindnesses.</b> My merits have diminished through the kindnesses and the truth that You have done with me — therefore I am afraid: perhaps, since You promised me, I have become corrupted by sin and it will cause me to be delivered into the hand of Esau (Shabbat 32)." "<b>And from all the truth.</b> The truth of Your words — that You kept for me all the promises You promised me." "<b>For with my staff.</b> I had with me neither silver nor gold nor livestock — only my staff alone. And from this [the Sages] said: he placed his staff in the Jordan and the Jordan split."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:42.471168231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}